    Since $\Delta^{0}=\bm{0}$ and $\varsigma^{0}(\tau)$ is proportional to $(1+\alpha\gamma^{0})^{\tau}$,
    \begin{gather} \sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1+\alpha\gamma^{0})^{t-\tau}\varsigma^{0}(\tau)=t\varsigma^{0}(t).
    \end{gather}
    Therefore, on the event in \eqref{eq: Set B to C and Delta} and $\mathcal{E}_{B}^{0,t+1}$,
